s hateful abusive and threatening  and we take the privacy of social media  influencers far more seriously than they  do themselves in many cases  we allow commentary critique and praise  of people who choose to monetize their  personal life as a business  anyone can join and post a comment and  we encourage people to report any that  overstep the line people that come to  post abusive or hateful content are  banned  m has spoken to mps publicly about the  abuse she's faced online she says she  was too scared to mention tattle life to  them afraid of facing a backlash from  users but now she wants to speak out and  put the damage they've caused under the  spotlight becky cottrell sky news
 

